# Azure Deployment and Feature Progress

## Feature Status
- [x] Additive SQLite schema for locale, OTP challenges, subscriptions, and payments
- [x] Signed-session authentication boundary and same-origin mutation checks
- [x] Server OTP generation, HMAC storage, expiration, rate limits, and attempt lockout
- [x] French email and five-language SMS delivery adapters
- [x] Server-side subscription expiry and monthly post-limit enforcement
- [x] Razorpay order, signature, webhook, cancellation, and receipt handling
- [x] Server-side payment window restriction: 05:00-10:59 IST
- [x] Settings, subscription, and post creation screens
- [x] ESLint passes with two existing image optimization warnings
- [x] TypeScript check passes
- [ ] Connect actual identity provider and trusted session issuer
- [ ] Configure Resend, Twilio, Razorpay, and verified user contacts
- [ ] Run production build after the active Next.js process releases `.next`

## Azure Deployment
- [x] Azure App Service plan updated for Node.js 24 and single-instance SQLite
- [ ] Subscription ID, resource group, and region supplied
- [ ] Azure CLI installed and authenticated in the user's terminal
- [ ] Bicep generated and validated
- [ ] Azure resources provisioned and app deployed
- [ ] Live endpoint and logs verified

## Blockers and Notes
- There is no sign-in UI/provider in this project. Protected routes reject requests until a trusted integration issues the signed `elevance_session` token.
- OTP and payment credentials are not configured in this workspace. The routes fail closed when required provider configuration is absent.
- Paid plans are 30-day payments with manual renewal after expiry; recurring billing is not configured.
- SQLite is local single-instance training storage, not suitable for multi-instance scale-out.
- Never commit `.env.local` or files in `data/*.db*`.